From 49aea71ddde623260fd1aef3a077c5ae3163e76e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel <2660793+imDaniel@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 18:04:46 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Package immutable attention profiles with explicit import
 provenance

Base: complete r6v author stack and downstream steering through 0187.
Rationale: preserve the imported attention-only schedule in a versioned
single-tensor envelope and exact manifest/directions materialization.
The format declares its attention extension and operator explicitly; full
and shared MLP schedules cannot be misread as this operator. Imported source
revisions, payload/schedule digests, license and converter identity remain
separate from unavailable extraction datasets. Extracted profiles require
all dataset identities. Preserve the adapted codec's MIT notice.
Bind model/tokenizer/template identities and exact manifest bytes, canonical
FP32 alpha schedule, immutable directions and file/directory equivalence.
Bundled hf:default/hf:NAME selection checks the strict index, size, SHA and
embedded name; it operates on a verified local release without network IO.
Quality: source directions and attention writer boundaries are unchanged.
Zero-alpha layers remain stock, including non-finite writer bit patterns.
Validation: 83 CPU contracts passed; 25 CUDA checks require the new image.
Source import/pack/materialize/index round trip passed on the pinned inputs.
Upstream status: independent downstream experiment; not submitted upstream.
